      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkaspectframe.c"
           line="32">The #GtkAspectFrame is useful when you want
pack a widget so that it can resize but always retains
the same aspect ratio. For instance, one might be
drawing a small preview of a larger image. #GtkAspectFrame
derives from #GtkFrame, so it can draw a label and
a frame around the child. The frame will be
"shrink-wrapped" to the size of the child.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkaspectframe.h" line="66"/>
      <implements name="Atk.ImplementorIface"/>
      <implements name="Buildable"/>
