      </method>
      <method name="remove" c:identifier="gtk_container_remove">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkcontainer.c"
             line="1211">Removes @widget from @container. @widget must be inside @container.
Note that @container will own a reference to @widget, and that this
may be the last reference held; so removing a widget from its
container can destroy that widget. If you want to use @widget
again, you need to add a reference to it while it's not inside
a container, using g_object_ref(). If you don't want to use @widget
again it's usually more efficient to simply destroy it directly
using gtk_widget_destroy() since this will remove it from the
container and help break any circular reference count cycles.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkcontainer.h"
                         line="113"/>
