      <glib:signal name="create-window" when="last" version="2.12">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtknotebook.c"
             line="989">The ::create-window signal is emitted when a detachable
tab is dropped on the root window.

A handler for this signal can create a window containing
a notebook where the tab will be attached. It is also
responsible for moving/resizing the window and adding the
necessary properties to the notebook (e.g. the
#GtkNotebook:group ).

The default handler uses the global window creation hook,
if one has been set with gtk_notebook_set_window_creation_hook().</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtknotebook.c"
