        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkrange.c"
             line="774">Sets the update policy for the range. #GTK_UPDATE_CONTINUOUS means that
anytime the range slider is moved, the range value will change and the
value_changed signal will be emitted. #GTK_UPDATE_DELAYED means that
the value will be updated after a brief timeout where no slider motion
occurs, so updates are spaced by a short time rather than
continuous. #GTK_UPDATE_DISCONTINUOUS means that the value will only
be updated when the user releases the button and ends the slider
drag operation.</doc>
        <doc-deprecated xml:space="preserve">There is no replacement. If you require delayed
  updates, you need to code it yourself.</doc-deprecated>
