      <method name="create_mark" c:identifier="gtk_text_buffer_create_mark">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextbuffer.c"
             line="2061">Creates a mark at position @where. If @mark_name is %NULL, the mark
is anonymous; otherwise, the mark can be retrieved by name using
gtk_text_buffer_get_mark(). If a mark has left gravity, and text is
inserted at the mark's current location, the mark will be moved to
the left of the newly-inserted text. If the mark has right gravity
(@left_gravity = %FALSE), the mark will end up on the right of
newly-inserted text. The standard left-to-right cursor is a mark
with right gravity (when you type, the cursor stays on the right
side of the text you're typing).

The caller of this function does &lt;emphasis&gt;not&lt;/emphasis&gt; own a
reference to the returned #GtkTextMark, so you can ignore the
return value if you like. Marks are owned by the buffer and go
away when the buffer does.

Emits the "mark-set" signal as notification of the mark's initial
placement.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextbuffer.h"
                         line="259"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextbuffer.c"
               line="2086">the new #GtkTextMark object</doc>
