      <method name="backward_line" c:identifier="gtk_text_iter_backward_line">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextiter.c"
             line="2521">Moves @iter to the start of the previous line. Returns %TRUE if
@iter could be moved; i.e. if @iter was at character offset 0, this
function returns %FALSE. Therefore if @iter was already on line 0,
but not at the start of the line, @iter is snapped to the start of
the line and the function returns %TRUE. (Note that this implies that
in a loop calling this function, the line number may not change on
every iteration, if your first iteration is on line 0.)</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextiter.h" line="184"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextiter.c"
