      <constructor name="new" c:identifier="gtk_text_mark_new" version="2.12">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextmark.c"
             line="189">Creates a text mark. Add it to a buffer using gtk_text_buffer_add_mark().
If @name is %NULL, the mark is anonymous; otherwise, the mark can be
retrieved by name using gtk_text_buffer_get_mark(). If a mark has left
gravity, and text is inserted at the mark's current location, the mark
will be moved to the left of the newly-inserted text. If the mark has
right gravity (@left_gravity = %FALSE), the mark will end up on the
right of newly-inserted text. The standard left-to-right cursor is a
mark with right gravity (when you type, the cursor stays on the right
side of the text you're typing).</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextmark.h" line="95"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktextmark.c"
