        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktreeview.c"
             line="11636">Scrolls the tree view such that the top-left corner of the visible
area is @tree_x, @tree_y, where @tree_x and @tree_y are specified
in tree coordinates.  The @tree_view must be realized before
this function is called.  If it isn't, you probably want to be
using gtk_tree_view_scroll_to_cell().

If either @tree_x or @tree_y are -1, then that direction isn't scrolled.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktreeview.h" line="201"/>
