      <method name="set_column_drag_function"
              c:identifier="gtk_tree_view_set_column_drag_function">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktreeview.c"
             line="11603">Sets a user function for determining where a column may be dropped when
dragged.  This function is called on every column pair in turn at the
beginning of a column drag to determine where a drop can take place.  The
arguments passed to @func are: the @tree_view, the #GtkTreeViewColumn being
dragged, the two #GtkTreeViewColumn s determining the drop spot, and
@user_data.  If either of the #GtkTreeViewColumn arguments for the drop spot
are %NULL, then they indicate an edge.  If @func is set to be %NULL, then
@tree_view reverts to the default behavior of allowing all columns to be
dropped everywhere.</doc>
