      <method name="grab_focus" c:identifier="gtk_widget_grab_focus">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkwidget.c"
             line="5309">Causes @widget to have the keyboard focus for the #GtkWindow it's
inside. @widget must be a focusable widget, such as a #GtkEntry;
something like #GtkFrame won't work.

More precisely, it must have the %GTK_CAN_FOCUS flag set. Use
gtk_widget_set_can_focus() to modify that flag.

The widget also needs to be realized and mapped. This is indicated by the
related signals. Grabbing the focus immediately after creating the widget
will likely fail and cause critical warnings.</doc>
