    <function name="init_check" c:identifier="gtk_init_check">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtkmain.c"
           line="984">This function does the same work as gtk_init() with only
a single change: It does not terminate the program if the GUI can't be
initialized. Instead it returns %FALSE on failure.

This way the application can fall back to some other means of communication
with the user - for example a curses or command line interface.</doc>
