    <function name="test_widget_click"
              c:identifier="gtk_test_widget_click"
              version="2.14">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktestutils.c"
           line="144">This function will generate a @button click (button press and button
release event) in the middle of the first GdkWindow found that belongs
to @widget.
For %GTK_NO_WINDOW widgets like GtkButton, this will often be an
input-only event window. For other widgets, this is usually widget-&gt;window.
Certain caveats should be considered when using this function, in
particular because the mouse pointer is warped to the button click
location, see gdk_test_simulate_button() for details.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk+-2.24.33/gtk/gtktestutils.h" line="53"/>
      <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
